Warden has no third-party dependencies. It compiles and runs against the JDK alone,
and the visual-QA harness (scripts/visual-qa.mjs) runs on Node's standard library and
speaks CDP to a browser already installed on the host. Nothing is vendored here, so
this file carries no third-party attributions.

The vendor CLIs Warden dispatches to (for example `codex`, `claude`, `grok`) are not
part of this distribution, are not redistributed with it, and are governed by their own
licences and terms of service. Warden invokes whatever the operator has installed and
configured under `~/.warden/profiles/`.
